### Your own tests

Write unit tests for what you build, beside your sources as `src/**/*.test.ts`.
`npm test` runs them in process with Vitest, in Node, with coverage measured over
`src/`.
{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
A test drives the game over its own clock for a counted number of frames, so it
needs no browser, and `@napi-rs/canvas` is installed for a test that wants a real
2D context.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
A test stands the engine up over its own canvas and clock and advances the game a
counted number of frames, so it needs no browser.
{{else}}
A test stands the engine up over a canvas from `@napi-rs/canvas` and a surface
and clock of its own, then advances the game a counted number of frames with
`engine.advance`, so it needs no browser.
{{/if}}

